WEBVTT

00:09.092 --> 00:11.094
[radio chatter]

00:16.474 --> 00:18.476
[soldier]
Did he try
to break it for you?

00:22.063 --> 00:24.065
[chatter stops]

00:32.949 --> 00:35.952
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:06.858 --> 01:08.109
[door opens]

01:22.123 --> 01:24.666
Your soldiers
are loyal to you.

01:24.667 --> 01:27.002
I think they're worried
we're gonna execute you.

01:27.003 --> 01:29.588
If I was getting executed,
Isaac would've come himself.

01:29.589 --> 01:31.006
There was a shooting
near the borderline

01:31.007 --> 01:32.424
between us and the Scars.

01:32.425 --> 01:35.219
Treaty might be broken.
He's dealing with that now.

01:35.220 --> 01:37.221
If it's war again, we're gonna
need all the soldiers we have.

01:37.222 --> 01:39.181
So he's wondering
why you apparently killed

01:39.182 --> 01:40.475
some of your own men.

01:42.227 --> 01:43.645
[Park] Including Leon.

01:45.897 --> 01:46.898
Leon?

01:49.025 --> 01:50.026
Leon.

01:51.361 --> 01:52.362
[Hanrahan]
Jesus.

01:56.241 --> 01:58.243
- [lighter flicks]
- What happened?

02:02.831 --> 02:05.541
- My unit is responsible for--
- Securing the hospital.

02:05.542 --> 02:07.126
I know your orders.
I gave them, Elise.

02:07.127 --> 02:08.878
What happened?

02:13.174 --> 02:15.426
We cleared the ground floor
up to the sixth.

02:16.553 --> 02:18.053
A few scattered
infected here or there.

02:18.054 --> 02:19.388
Nothing we
couldn't handle.

02:19.389 --> 02:21.640
All that was left
was the basement.

02:21.641 --> 02:23.392
B1, B2, B3.

02:23.393 --> 02:24.893
We were expecting the worst,

02:24.894 --> 02:26.145
the kind of environment
they like.

02:26.146 --> 02:27.896
Plus, the old-timers said
that down there

02:27.897 --> 02:30.816
was where they brought
the first Cordyceps patients
in '03.

02:30.817 --> 02:32.735
On top of that,
we had an access problem.

02:34.070 --> 02:38.073
These stairwells here,
here, and here caved in,

02:38.074 --> 02:40.075
and all the elevator cars
were stuck in their shafts

02:40.076 --> 02:41.493
just below ground level.

02:41.494 --> 02:42.953
The only way in or out
of the basement

02:42.954 --> 02:44.747
is here, this stairwell.

02:46.040 --> 02:48.877
So yesterday, that's where
I sent a squad, down to B1.

02:49.878 --> 02:51.421
- And?
- Nothing.

02:52.422 --> 02:54.424
The whole floor was empty,
not even rats.

02:55.091 --> 02:57.509
So today, B2,
hoping for more of the same,

02:57.510 --> 02:59.094
I sent another squad down,

02:59.095 --> 03:01.389
and I put Leon
in charge 'cause...

03:04.267 --> 03:05.476
he's my best.

03:08.021 --> 03:09.938
A few minutes in,
he radios back.

03:09.939 --> 03:12.274
There's Cordyceps
on the walls, the floor.

03:12.275 --> 03:14.318
Chances are,
they'll find infected next,

03:14.319 --> 03:15.986
but that's what they
were down there for,

03:15.987 --> 03:17.779
so I told him to proceed.

03:17.780 --> 03:19.781
Five minutes later,
he radios again.

03:19.782 --> 03:21.117
This time, he...

03:24.621 --> 03:26.080
he was struggling
to breathe.

03:27.916 --> 03:29.083
He could hardly talk.

03:32.921 --> 03:35.965
I thought maybe
he had been bit.

03:37.175 --> 03:39.427
I said,
"Leon, were you bit?"
He said...

03:42.138 --> 03:43.514
He said, "It's in the air."

03:45.058 --> 03:47.142
[♪ faint ominous music playing]

03:47.143 --> 03:48.937
He said, "It's in the air.

03:50.313 --> 03:51.397
Seal us in."

03:56.694 --> 03:58.153
And I knew
it wasn't in the vents,

03:58.154 --> 04:00.155
or we would've all
been infected weeks ago.

04:00.156 --> 04:01.907
So, I scrambled
my other team

04:01.908 --> 04:03.742
and we locked
the only door to B2,

04:03.743 --> 04:05.495
and we locked the only
door to B1.

04:06.871 --> 04:08.289
And we did what Leon said.

04:11.584 --> 04:12.919
We sealed them in.

04:18.633 --> 04:20.593
[Hanrahan]
Nothing else has gotten out?

04:21.844 --> 04:23.346
No one else has gotten sick?

04:25.390 --> 04:26.474
Okay.

04:27.475 --> 04:29.852
The hospital's a resource
we can't afford to lose.

04:32.522 --> 04:34.356
I'll inform only the people
who absolutely

04:34.357 --> 04:35.691
need to know,
and no one else.

04:35.692 --> 04:37.734
As far as I'm concerned,
Sergeant Park,

04:37.735 --> 04:39.611
you resolved the situation
permanently

04:39.612 --> 04:41.072
and heroically.

04:42.657 --> 04:44.367
We owe you a debt.

04:54.127 --> 04:56.045
I'm sorry about your son.

05:03.136 --> 05:06.139
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

06:06.074 --> 06:07.325
[♪ theme concludes]

06:09.911 --> 06:11.036
[birdsong]

06:11.037 --> 06:13.081
[distant explosion booming]

06:17.585 --> 06:19.878
[distant gunfire]

06:19.879 --> 06:21.923
[radio static]

06:26.302 --> 06:29.304
[W.L.F. soldier] [over radio]
Patrol 14 heading north
to 13th and Bradford.

06:29.305 --> 06:30.972
One mile out.

06:30.973 --> 06:32.974
[W.L.F. soldier 2]
One mile out. Copy.

06:32.975 --> 06:34.644
Mobile three.

06:35.311 --> 06:36.478
[W.L.F. soldier 3]
Mobile three.

06:36.479 --> 06:40.400
[indistinct radio chatter
continues]

06:42.652 --> 06:43.985
[W.L.F. soldier 1]
Possible movement

06:43.986 --> 06:45.487
at the convention center.

06:45.488 --> 06:48.031
- [electricity buzzing]
- [Ellie sighs]

06:48.032 --> 06:50.867
Ta-da!

06:50.868 --> 06:52.702
- What?
- Lights.

06:52.703 --> 06:54.329
Oh, good.

06:54.330 --> 06:55.872
They have a big-ass
generator down there.

06:55.873 --> 06:57.458
Natural gas, baby.

06:59.877 --> 07:02.170
- You figure it out yet?
- Gettin' there.

07:02.171 --> 07:04.882
You'll find a safe way
to get us to the hospital
though, right?

07:09.178 --> 07:10.346
[chuckles]

07:11.973 --> 07:13.515
Can I help?

07:13.516 --> 07:15.560
Um... no.

07:16.144 --> 07:17.936
Why, because I'm stupid?

07:17.937 --> 07:19.271
That's not the word
I would use.

07:19.272 --> 07:20.648
Really?
What word then?

07:22.066 --> 07:23.358
Non-school-oriented.

07:23.359 --> 07:25.486
Fuck you, I went to school.
Let me help.

07:28.906 --> 07:31.199
I'm triangulating.

07:31.200 --> 07:32.951
- Do you know how that works?
- Yes.

07:32.952 --> 07:34.370
With triangles.

07:35.580 --> 07:36.788
It's pretty standard.

07:36.789 --> 07:39.040
I get a bearing of
their troop movements,

07:39.041 --> 07:40.542
and then triangulate
back to their bases.

07:40.543 --> 07:42.085
I'm estimating angles, though.

07:42.086 --> 07:44.463
I mean, if I had a protractor,
it would be a lot more accurate.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.465
Oh, I actually brought
a protractor.

07:46.466 --> 07:48.176
- You did?
- No.

07:48.759 --> 07:50.552
I don't know what that is,
and I hated math.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.429
I'm gonna
leave you alone now
and go and explore

07:52.430 --> 07:54.764
the rest of this place,
because you're smart as fuck

07:54.765 --> 07:56.142
and you're figuring it out.

07:58.144 --> 08:00.563
- Ellie.
- Yes?

08:04.984 --> 08:06.527
[chuckles]

08:08.070 --> 08:10.072
- [walkie beeps]
- [radio static]

08:17.747 --> 08:19.207
[door opens]

08:38.684 --> 08:41.687
[♪ gentle music playing]

08:53.407 --> 08:55.409
♪

09:34.323 --> 09:36.325
[♪ strums guitar]

09:37.535 --> 09:39.537
[tuning guitar]

09:48.504 --> 09:50.506
[♪ playing melody]

09:58.556 --> 10:01.976
[softly singing]
♪ If I ever were to lose you ♪

10:03.644 --> 10:05.646
[♪ stops playing]

10:09.567 --> 10:12.570
[low rumbling]

10:20.786 --> 10:22.413
[sighs]

10:26.500 --> 10:28.044
[door opens]

10:31.964 --> 10:33.299
Did you figure it out?

10:34.508 --> 10:36.385
- I think so, yeah.
- [door closes loudly]

10:37.553 --> 10:38.554
Good.

10:39.722 --> 10:43.224
[Dina]
We follow a safe path
west until this spot.

10:43.225 --> 10:45.353
Here, let me show you.

10:46.520 --> 10:50.231
They run a line of patrols
north and south, like this.

10:50.232 --> 10:51.733
They're pretty evenly
spread out,

10:51.734 --> 10:54.402
so they're watching
that entire area.

10:54.403 --> 10:57.113
But there's a gap
between here and here.

10:57.114 --> 11:00.116
Now, on this map,
do you see this
long-ass building?

11:00.117 --> 11:01.409
Mm-hmm, yeah.

11:01.410 --> 11:05.413
So, we cut through
and slip by.

11:05.414 --> 11:07.666
What is that
long-ass building?

11:07.667 --> 11:09.084
No clue.

11:09.085 --> 11:10.794
But it's set off
from the residential area,

11:10.795 --> 11:12.754
so maybe it's a warehouse
or something.

11:12.755 --> 11:15.131
It's a big fucking something
for them just to ignore.

11:15.132 --> 11:16.633
Why aren't they patrolling it?

11:16.634 --> 11:17.802
[Dina sighs]

11:18.761 --> 11:21.429
- Infected.
- Probably.

11:21.430 --> 11:23.682
If we make it through,

11:23.683 --> 11:25.183
we pop out
behind their patrols.

11:25.184 --> 11:28.019
The hospital's maybe
a quarter mile from there.

11:28.020 --> 11:29.771
Nora should be
on the first floor,

11:29.772 --> 11:31.147
far end of the North Wing.

11:31.148 --> 11:32.941
Wait, how the fuck
do you know that?

11:32.942 --> 11:35.026
They never shut up.
I hear everything.

11:35.027 --> 11:37.278
Morons.
Middle of a fucking war,

11:37.279 --> 11:38.947
and they're just broadcasting
their positions.

11:38.948 --> 11:40.365
Yeah, so I've been
thinking about that.

11:40.366 --> 11:42.617
You know these people
they're fighting, the Scars?

11:42.618 --> 11:44.661
We already know they use
bows and arrows, right?

11:44.662 --> 11:47.622
And they seem culty,
or at least really religious.

11:47.623 --> 11:50.458
- You ever hear of Amish people?
- Amish people? No.

11:50.459 --> 11:53.628
Well, they were around back
in '03, Pennsylvania mostly.

11:53.629 --> 11:55.964
But they chose to live
like it was the 1800s.

11:55.965 --> 11:59.175
Maybe the Scars are like that?
No electricity or technology.

11:59.176 --> 12:02.137
Because these motherfuckers
talk on the radio

12:02.138 --> 12:03.973
like they know
no one's listening.

12:04.765 --> 12:07.308
Yeah, and they didn't care
that a walkie was missing.

12:07.309 --> 12:08.977
It's good.
They're overconfident.

12:08.978 --> 12:11.147
- It gives us an edge.
- It does.

12:12.189 --> 12:14.065
But what we're
doing is reckless,

12:14.066 --> 12:16.234
so kind of a wash.

12:16.235 --> 12:18.487
[indistinct radio chatter
continues]

12:19.655 --> 12:21.364
If we were to leave now,
it'd be dark by the time

12:21.365 --> 12:23.408
we got to the big
fucking something, right?

12:23.409 --> 12:24.535
Mm-hmm.

12:25.619 --> 12:27.621
[distant seagulls cawing]

12:28.330 --> 12:29.707
[Ellie sighs]

12:31.834 --> 12:33.294
Let's go be reckless.

12:34.545 --> 12:37.548
[♪ dramatic music playing]

12:44.096 --> 12:46.098
[distant explosion booming]

12:58.736 --> 13:01.279
Are you sure
this way is safe?

13:01.280 --> 13:02.448
You don't trust me?

13:03.365 --> 13:05.283
I trust you.
I don't trust Seattle.

13:05.284 --> 13:07.619
Me neither, but let's just talk
like everything's fine

13:07.620 --> 13:09.788
because if I get too anxious,
I'm gonna barf again.

13:09.789 --> 13:11.748
[Ellie]
Alright, how 'bout this?

13:11.749 --> 13:13.374
What are you
gonna name it?

13:13.375 --> 13:14.418
Huh?

13:15.711 --> 13:18.713
Oh, uh, if it's a girl, Ellie.

13:18.714 --> 13:21.049
If it's a boy, Elijah.

13:21.050 --> 13:22.634
- Really?
- No.

13:22.635 --> 13:24.011
Why?
It's a cool name.

13:25.221 --> 13:26.554
What the fuck?

13:26.555 --> 13:28.640
[insects buzzing]

13:28.641 --> 13:30.684
[♪ ominous music playing]

13:39.902 --> 13:41.945
[Dina retching]

13:41.946 --> 13:43.989
[insects buzzing]

13:48.828 --> 13:50.453
We shouldn't be here.

13:50.454 --> 13:52.330
We shouldn't have come,
I shouldn't have
dragged you here.

13:52.331 --> 13:55.250
You're having a fucking baby.
What am I doing?

13:55.251 --> 13:57.586
Dina, do you wanna go back?

13:58.170 --> 14:00.464
I'll take you back.
You don't need
to do this with me.

14:02.550 --> 14:04.552
Oh, I'm so fucking stupid.

14:05.427 --> 14:07.429
[Ellie breathing heavily]

14:13.269 --> 14:15.812
You know, you never asked me
about the first person I killed.

14:15.813 --> 14:17.480
[Ellie] Huh?

14:17.481 --> 14:19.275
Okay. Who?

14:20.192 --> 14:22.193
When I was little,
we lived in a cabin

14:22.194 --> 14:25.030
in a forest
north of Santa Fe.

14:25.531 --> 14:28.032
And there were
scattered families around,

14:28.033 --> 14:29.702
but mostly it
was just us alone.

14:31.078 --> 14:33.162
And I would get so bored
cooped up with my mom

14:33.163 --> 14:34.455
and sister,
I would just beg them,

14:34.456 --> 14:36.207
"Just let me play outside."

14:36.208 --> 14:37.792
But my mom was scared

14:37.793 --> 14:39.837
and she wouldn't let me
go outside alone.

14:40.838 --> 14:42.630
But one day,
I just fucking did,

14:42.631 --> 14:44.465
and I had a gun,
so who's gonna
fuck with me?

14:44.466 --> 14:46.467
Now, you already know
how this story ends

14:46.468 --> 14:50.471
because I don't live in a cabin
north of Santa Fe anymore,

14:50.472 --> 14:52.474
and I don't have a mom
or sister anymore.

14:53.183 --> 14:54.893
But since everyone's
past is fucked

14:54.894 --> 14:57.061
and we've all heard
everyone's fucked stories,

14:57.062 --> 14:59.480
how do you think
this one goes?

14:59.481 --> 15:01.816
I don't know.
Uh, Raiders?

15:01.817 --> 15:04.278
Just one.
And then?

15:04.862 --> 15:07.155
Uh, you got home.

15:07.156 --> 15:09.324
They were dead,
he was gone.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.493
Almost.
He was still there.

15:12.536 --> 15:15.496
I heard them screaming
and I ran back with my gun out

15:15.497 --> 15:17.582
but I was too slow
because I was fucking eight.

15:17.583 --> 15:19.667
And when he heard me,
he turned around,

15:19.668 --> 15:21.128
and he looked really startled.

15:22.254 --> 15:25.006
And when I shot him,
he looked more...

15:25.007 --> 15:26.507
startled.

15:26.508 --> 15:28.509
Fuck, I'm so sorry.

15:28.510 --> 15:30.511
I didn't know,
I thought...

15:30.512 --> 15:32.389
- How did you get to Jackson?
- It doesn't matter.

15:33.599 --> 15:35.351
This is what matters.

15:36.769 --> 15:39.437
Whatever reason
Joel gave those people
to do what they did,

15:39.438 --> 15:41.273
he didn't deserve that.

15:42.024 --> 15:45.486
And I think,
what if I hadn't snuck out?

15:46.904 --> 15:48.780
What if my mom and sister

15:48.781 --> 15:50.699
were beaten to death
in front of me?

15:51.283 --> 15:53.953
What if that motherfucker
made me watch as he did it?

15:55.329 --> 15:56.871
Would it make a difference
if my family

15:56.872 --> 15:58.290
had hurt his people first?

16:00.167 --> 16:01.168
No.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.046
No.

16:05.673 --> 16:07.341
And if I hadn't killed him...

16:08.509 --> 16:10.219
if he had gotten away...

16:11.387 --> 16:14.556
I promise you, I would have
hunted him down forever.

16:16.183 --> 16:17.518
Forever.

16:20.145 --> 16:22.147
[♪ soft, melancholy
music playing]

16:35.119 --> 16:36.870
I'll go back, if you want.

16:38.747 --> 16:40.791
And I'll keep going,
if you want.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.252
There's no right answer.

16:44.044 --> 16:45.587
If I die, it's on me.

16:47.006 --> 16:48.965
It won't be your fault.

16:48.966 --> 16:50.509
So, what do you want to do?

16:52.511 --> 16:55.848
[♪ soft, melancholy
music continues]

17:02.396 --> 17:03.981
[whispering]
Keep going.

17:15.367 --> 17:17.285
[♪ dramatic music playing]

17:17.286 --> 17:19.288
[dog barking]

17:29.673 --> 17:31.842
- [Dina] Do you see anything?
- No. Let's go.

17:41.226 --> 17:42.770
[Ellie]
Hurry! Down, down, down.

17:45.606 --> 17:47.315
[vehicle rumbling]

17:47.316 --> 17:48.567
Cover me.

17:49.651 --> 17:52.654
[♪ dramatic music
continues playing]

18:01.497 --> 18:03.499
[metal rattling]

18:17.805 --> 18:20.808
[rustling]

18:21.934 --> 18:23.936
[banging]

18:38.992 --> 18:41.077
At least
we're not blocked in.

18:41.078 --> 18:42.537
And there are
two more positives.

18:42.538 --> 18:45.456
The search lights are up high
to scan the outside,

18:45.457 --> 18:47.458
which means there'll be
no line of sight to the inside.

18:47.459 --> 18:49.837
Good.
What's the other positive?

18:51.713 --> 18:54.257
That door's open,
and nothing's come out

18:54.258 --> 18:56.050
to kill us... yet.

18:56.051 --> 18:58.137
- Great.
- Maybe.

18:59.429 --> 19:01.973
- I'm gonna take a peek.
- Yeah, you should do that,

19:01.974 --> 19:03.767
because you're the one
who can't get infected.

19:16.321 --> 19:17.781
[Dina]
How's it look?

19:20.617 --> 19:22.160
Haunted, but empty.

19:22.161 --> 19:23.954
Oh, just like us.

19:25.122 --> 19:28.291
Look, I'm not saying
there won't be infected
somewhere in there.

19:28.292 --> 19:31.252
In fact, there's no fucking way
this entire place is empty.

19:31.253 --> 19:33.505
But simple logic, it's not
gonna be a horde, right?

19:35.966 --> 19:38.092
We're not underground,
and the Wolves

19:38.093 --> 19:40.470
are right next door
with their vehicles
and lights.

19:41.513 --> 19:44.140
A horde's not gonna
ignore that shit.

19:44.141 --> 19:45.975
So what, we've got maybe

19:45.976 --> 19:48.978
a few strays
and a couple clickers?

19:48.979 --> 19:51.480
We can handle that.
We've done it
like a million times.

19:51.481 --> 19:54.108
Yeah.
We'll be okay.

19:54.109 --> 19:56.944
But shooting
has to be a last resort, okay?

19:56.945 --> 19:58.654
Because if the Wolves
hear gunfire,

19:58.655 --> 20:00.823
- then we'll have
a whole army up our ass.
- Fine.

20:00.824 --> 20:02.992
- Ellie.
- What?

20:02.993 --> 20:05.494
If it gets bad,
and we have to make a choice

20:05.495 --> 20:08.289
between shooting or running,
we run.

20:08.290 --> 20:10.417
Last resort, I got it.

20:13.253 --> 20:14.962
Oh, you think
that no matter
what happens,

20:14.963 --> 20:16.339
I'm just gonna start firing?

20:16.340 --> 20:17.965
Literally every single time.
Yes.

20:17.966 --> 20:20.801
Don't get angry.
You're a little crazy.

20:20.802 --> 20:22.220
And that's exciting.

20:22.221 --> 20:23.471
It's one of the reasons
I love you.

20:23.472 --> 20:25.766
But I do wanna
make it out of here.

20:27.559 --> 20:28.810
You love me?

20:32.022 --> 20:34.066
[♪ gentle music playing]

20:36.693 --> 20:38.028
- I re--
- Oh, I know.

20:42.115 --> 20:44.284
So, tell me again,
what's the plan?

20:46.119 --> 20:47.329
Knives or run.

20:49.748 --> 20:51.124
Okay, Crazy.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.752
- [knife unsheathing]
- Here we go.

20:56.129 --> 20:58.131
[distant dog barking]

21:00.425 --> 21:02.094
[door squeaking]

21:04.972 --> 21:06.974
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

21:11.770 --> 21:13.772
[water dripping]

21:21.280 --> 21:22.823
So far, so good.

21:29.454 --> 21:30.622
W-- wait.

21:34.293 --> 21:35.919
[whispering]
Do you hear something?

21:44.636 --> 21:45.637
No.

21:51.727 --> 21:53.270
So, this way then?

21:54.896 --> 21:55.897
Yeah.

22:09.995 --> 22:11.997
[door squeaking open]

22:25.135 --> 22:27.596
[Dina]
Lots of windows in here.
Let's be careful.

22:30.182 --> 22:31.183
Okay.

22:32.351 --> 22:35.354
[♪ tense music playing]

22:53.330 --> 22:54.331
Dina.

22:59.336 --> 23:00.545
[mysterious gasping]

23:06.593 --> 23:07.886
[mysterious breathing]

23:10.764 --> 23:13.057
What the fuck is that?
And why is it hiding?

23:13.058 --> 23:15.017
I think it's a smart one,

23:15.018 --> 23:16.852
like the one that stalked me
at the supermarket.

23:16.853 --> 23:18.396
Okay, but you
killed that one,

23:18.397 --> 23:19.855
so we can kill
this one too, right?

23:19.856 --> 23:22.483
Yes, I killed it.
Not before it got me.

23:22.484 --> 23:24.568
- It fucking bit you?
- What was I supposed
to do, tell you?

23:24.569 --> 23:27.738
- You would've--
- [stalker vocalizing]

23:27.739 --> 23:29.698
Listen, if it's like
the other one,

23:29.699 --> 23:31.742
it's gonna be fast
and it's gonna be sneaky.

23:31.743 --> 23:33.661
But this time,
it's two on one.

23:33.662 --> 23:35.996
Now, that fucker's
gonna try to flank us,

23:35.997 --> 23:38.165
so I say we flank it first.

23:38.166 --> 23:41.168
We split up.
Whichever one it follows,

23:41.169 --> 23:43.170
the other one comes up
and takes it out from behind.

23:43.171 --> 23:44.214
Plan?

23:47.050 --> 23:48.342
Plan.

23:48.343 --> 23:49.970
[stalker vocalizing]

23:54.266 --> 23:56.268
[stalker grunting]

23:58.270 --> 23:59.771
[screeching lightly]

24:01.231 --> 24:02.189
[both gasp]

24:02.190 --> 24:03.733
- What do we do?
- I don't know.

24:04.651 --> 24:05.902
Let's go back
the way we came.

24:06.820 --> 24:09.072
If we run,
they're gonna chase
so we have to go slow.

24:13.201 --> 24:14.369
[stalker vocalizing]

24:15.912 --> 24:17.538
[Ellie and Dina panting]

24:17.539 --> 24:19.416
[infected grunting]

24:20.876 --> 24:23.544
You see that fencing over there?
I'm gonna lure as many as I can.

24:23.545 --> 24:25.045
You're gonna run in there,
secure the gate,

24:25.046 --> 24:26.547
secure it however you can,
and stay in there.

24:26.548 --> 24:28.632
Dina.
I can get bit a lot.

24:28.633 --> 24:30.635
- [infected shouting]
- You can't. Do as I say.

24:32.387 --> 24:33.388
Go!

24:34.556 --> 24:38.101
- [infected shouting]
- [gunshots]

24:39.561 --> 24:41.729
[Dina panting]

24:41.730 --> 24:44.232
[infected screaming]

24:45.025 --> 24:46.567
[Dina shouting]

24:46.568 --> 24:48.320
- [gunshot]
- [infected grunting]

24:49.821 --> 24:52.073
[infected continues shouting]

24:54.701 --> 24:55.702
[gunshots]

24:59.122 --> 25:00.998
[distant gunshots]

25:00.999 --> 25:02.042
[grunting]

25:02.626 --> 25:03.792
[stalker snarling]

25:03.793 --> 25:04.836
[Ellie screaming]

25:07.631 --> 25:08.797
[gunshots]

25:08.798 --> 25:09.925
[gun clicking]

25:10.175 --> 25:12.719
- [infected continue shouting]
- [Dina whimpering]

25:17.140 --> 25:19.142
- [stalker snarling]
- [Ellie screaming]

25:22.812 --> 25:25.524
[gunshots]

25:27.400 --> 25:29.860
[gunshots continue]

25:29.861 --> 25:31.821
[sound muffed]

25:38.078 --> 25:40.080
[muffled panting]

25:47.379 --> 25:49.630
- Did you get bit?
- What? No.

25:49.631 --> 25:51.006
[Dina]
She's okay.

25:51.007 --> 25:53.385
I was watching.
They didn't bite her.

25:54.219 --> 25:56.054
- Jesse, I swear.
- [distant infected screeching]

25:57.514 --> 25:58.556
We gotta go.

25:58.557 --> 26:02.476
[♪ tense music playing]

26:02.477 --> 26:04.311
[W.L.F. soldiers shouting
indistinctly]

26:04.312 --> 26:05.564
[W.L.F. soldier]
Move! Move! Move!

26:06.523 --> 26:08.983
[Jesse]
Don't stop! Keep going!

26:08.984 --> 26:10.818
- [gunshots]
- I'll shoot 'em! Go!

26:10.819 --> 26:12.152
[W.L.F. soldier 1]
Heading west!

26:12.153 --> 26:13.821
[W.L.F. soldier 2]
Over there! Over there!

26:13.822 --> 26:15.782
[gunfire]

26:16.741 --> 26:18.409
[gunfire continues]

26:18.410 --> 26:21.454
[♪ tense music continues]

26:25.750 --> 26:27.752
[all panting]

26:28.795 --> 26:29.837
[Jesse]
The park!

26:29.838 --> 26:32.299
We can lose 'em in there.
Come on!

26:33.133 --> 26:34.134
[gunshot]

26:38.430 --> 26:40.432
- [panting]
- [bushes rustling]

26:42.684 --> 26:44.351
[W.L.F. soldier 1]
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Stop. Stop.

26:44.352 --> 26:46.020
We don't go in there.

26:46.021 --> 26:47.896
[W.L.F. soldier 2]
Looks like five...
three unknowns,

26:47.897 --> 26:49.356
chased into the park.
Heavily armed.

26:49.357 --> 26:50.942
- Not Scars.
- [Ellie] What are they doing?

26:51.860 --> 26:54.361
[W.L.F. soldier 1]
If they try and come out,
shoot 'em.

26:54.362 --> 26:55.738
Not coming in the park.

26:55.739 --> 26:57.865
Oh, you gotta be kidding me.

26:57.866 --> 27:00.034
Great.
More infected.

27:00.035 --> 27:02.370
Maybe, but we can't
go back that way.

27:03.872 --> 27:04.956
Come on.

27:09.377 --> 27:10.378
[Ellie] Jesse.

27:12.881 --> 27:13.964
Jesse.

27:13.965 --> 27:15.758
- What?
- How did you find us?

27:15.759 --> 27:17.802
The map you left
in the theater.

27:18.887 --> 27:20.763
Impressive triangulation,
by the way.

27:20.764 --> 27:21.930
Thanks, that was all Dina.

27:21.931 --> 27:23.474
Trust me,
I didn't think it was you.

27:23.475 --> 27:24.933
How did you find the theater?

27:24.934 --> 27:26.811
Do I look like I wanna
fucking talk to you right now?

27:28.396 --> 27:29.980
You came alone?

27:29.981 --> 27:31.315
No. Me and Tommy.

27:31.316 --> 27:33.150
We split up when
we got to the city.

27:33.151 --> 27:35.569
- Cover more ground.
- I can't believe they
sent you after us.

27:35.570 --> 27:38.238
They didn't, but you two
were gonna die out here,

27:38.239 --> 27:40.574
so we snuck out the next night.
And it's a good thing we did.

27:40.575 --> 27:41.909
You know what,
we were doing
pretty fucking good

27:41.910 --> 27:43.411
- up until--
- Up until what?

27:43.995 --> 27:45.622
[owl hooting]

27:47.666 --> 27:49.291
Until we weren't.

27:49.292 --> 27:51.251
Is Tommy okay?

27:51.252 --> 27:52.836
Hopefully.

27:52.837 --> 27:54.421
We're supposed
to rendezvous in the morning.

27:54.422 --> 27:56.924
- [Dina] So, what now?
- [Jesse] Find a way out,

27:56.925 --> 27:58.634
get back to the theater,
shelter for the night.

27:58.635 --> 28:02.137
Meet up with Tommy,
and then we all go home.

28:02.138 --> 28:03.765
- No.
- [Dina] Ellie.

28:06.101 --> 28:09.019
[whistling in distance]

28:09.020 --> 28:10.772
[Dina] [whispering]
What the fuck is that?

28:12.565 --> 28:13.817
[whistling]

28:18.113 --> 28:21.116
[whistling continues]

28:30.041 --> 28:31.710
[softly] Hey. Go.

28:34.587 --> 28:37.590
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

28:43.680 --> 28:45.180
[W.L.F. soldier]
No, wait, please.

28:45.181 --> 28:46.515
Please, please, please!

28:46.516 --> 28:48.559
I'm not-- I'm not
like the others. Please.

28:48.560 --> 28:51.395
No, no, no, wait.
Wait, wait, I'll join!

28:51.396 --> 28:53.355
- I-- I'll join you. I'll join.
- [Seraphite] Too late, Wolf.

28:53.356 --> 28:55.232
[W.L.F. soldier]
No, no. No, no, no, wait!
I know things.

28:55.233 --> 28:57.317
I know what Isaac is planning.
I can help you. I can--

28:57.318 --> 28:59.403
[gasping]

28:59.404 --> 29:01.822
[Seraphite] We have
no interest in your words.

29:01.823 --> 29:04.324
"For the corrupted soul
knows only lies."

29:04.325 --> 29:05.534
So taught the Prophet.

29:05.535 --> 29:07.161
[all Seraphites]
May She guide us.

29:07.162 --> 29:09.747
No. No. No. No. No.

29:09.748 --> 29:11.040
[whimpering]

29:12.167 --> 29:14.835
No. No, no, no.
Please, please, please. No.

29:14.836 --> 29:16.837
No. No.
[sobbing]

29:16.838 --> 29:18.672
No! No! No!

29:18.673 --> 29:20.174
[whimpering]

29:20.175 --> 29:21.551
[sobbing] No.

29:24.304 --> 29:25.638
[fabric tearing]

29:26.723 --> 29:29.517
[soldier continues whimpering]

29:30.435 --> 29:31.685
Oh, please, please, no.

29:31.686 --> 29:33.187
[Seraphite]
He is nested in sin.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.688
- No, no.
- [all Seraphites] Free him,

29:34.689 --> 29:37.107
that he may know Her love.

29:37.108 --> 29:38.901
No, no.
No, no, no, no.

29:38.902 --> 29:40.611
Please, please, please, no.

29:40.612 --> 29:42.864
[sobbing]

29:43.907 --> 29:46.117
- [shouting]
- [flesh squelching]

29:49.370 --> 29:51.038
[blood pouring]

29:51.039 --> 29:53.416
[soldier gagging,
blood gurgling]

30:00.340 --> 30:01.548
Now, he is free.

30:01.549 --> 30:03.550
[whistling]

30:03.551 --> 30:05.135
- [arrow whooshing]
- [Dina grunting]

30:05.136 --> 30:06.970
- [Jesse] Oh, fuck!
- [Dina whimpering]

30:06.971 --> 30:09.390
[whistling]

30:10.391 --> 30:11.558
I'll lead them away.
Get her out.

30:11.559 --> 30:13.310
Go! I'll meet you
back at the theater.

30:13.311 --> 30:17.064
- Fucking go!
- [gunshots]

30:17.065 --> 30:19.441
You won't get away, Wolf.
She sees you.

30:19.442 --> 30:21.151
She watches over us all.

30:21.152 --> 30:24.822
[♪ tense, dramatic
music playing]

30:24.823 --> 30:26.407
- [whistling]
- [arrow whooshing]

30:31.079 --> 30:33.081
[Ellie panting]

30:33.957 --> 30:35.625
- [whistling]
- [arrow whooshing]

30:37.544 --> 30:40.296
- [Ellie grunting]
- [whistling]

30:45.260 --> 30:47.136
[whistling]

30:58.857 --> 31:00.107
[Seraphite]
He's not here.

31:00.108 --> 31:01.526
[whistling]

31:02.652 --> 31:05.112
[whistling]

31:05.113 --> 31:07.948
- May She guide us.
- May She guide us.

31:07.949 --> 31:10.493
[Seraphite]
Alright, spread out.
Keep moving.

31:23.756 --> 31:26.759
[♪ tense music playing]

32:00.752 --> 32:03.171
- [insects chirring]
- [dog panting]

32:05.173 --> 32:07.175
[indistinct radio chatter]

32:17.810 --> 32:19.812
[radio chatter continues]

32:28.488 --> 32:30.823
[leaves rustling]

32:31.908 --> 32:34.577
[dog growling, barking]

32:37.956 --> 32:39.456
[barking continues]

32:39.457 --> 32:41.124
[W.L.F. soldier] [over radio]
What do we got?

32:41.125 --> 32:43.210
Not sure.
Checking it out.

32:43.211 --> 32:45.045
- [dog growling]
- Come on, Bonnie.

32:45.046 --> 32:47.048
[Bonnie continues barking]

33:00.144 --> 33:02.145
[barking continues]

33:02.146 --> 33:04.065
[growling and barking]

33:09.529 --> 33:11.279
[W.L.F. soldier]
It was a critter or something.

33:11.280 --> 33:13.366
- All clear.
- [Bonnie barking]

33:15.952 --> 33:17.495
[distant barking continues]

33:20.581 --> 33:22.583
[scissors snipping]

33:23.793 --> 33:25.294
You're all set.

33:30.466 --> 33:32.552
[people chattering quietly]

33:41.185 --> 33:43.688
- [door closes]
- [fluorescent lights buzzing]

34:08.963 --> 34:10.465
[Ellie]
Put that shit down.

34:11.716 --> 34:13.551
Hands up.
Turn around.

34:24.103 --> 34:25.521
You remember me?

34:26.856 --> 34:28.399
Yeah, you remember me.

34:29.817 --> 34:32.445
- What do you want?
- Where's Abby?

34:33.571 --> 34:35.989
- I don't know.
- Yes, you do.

34:35.990 --> 34:38.575
You shoot me,
the sound will have
every soldier come running.

34:38.576 --> 34:40.036
You'll still be dead.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.291
Tell me where she is
and maybe I let you go.

34:47.210 --> 34:49.878
- We could've killed you.
- Maybe you should have.

34:49.879 --> 34:53.633
Or maybe you should've
stayed the fuck
out of Jackson, Nora.

34:55.051 --> 34:56.177
Where's Abby?

35:05.061 --> 35:06.979
I'm sorry you saw it happen.

35:09.273 --> 35:11.608
No one should ever have to see
something like that.

35:11.609 --> 35:14.194
- Stop it.
- Sometimes at night,

35:14.195 --> 35:16.864
I still hear his screams.

35:17.824 --> 35:21.202
It was a terrible thing,
the way he died.

35:22.453 --> 35:23.871
Yeah.

35:25.498 --> 35:27.542
Yeah, the little bitch
got what he deserved.

35:29.752 --> 35:31.962
[Ellie exclaiming]

35:31.963 --> 35:33.464
Motherfucker!

35:34.382 --> 35:35.632
Intruder!

35:35.633 --> 35:37.717
[♪ dramatic music playing]

35:37.718 --> 35:38.802
Intruder!

35:38.803 --> 35:39.846
[gunshot,
glass shattering]

35:40.388 --> 35:42.598
Hey! Shoot her!

35:44.392 --> 35:46.394
- [gunfire]
- [glass shattering]

35:47.395 --> 35:50.398
[♪ dramatic music continues]

35:53.276 --> 35:54.777
[grunting]

36:01.450 --> 36:03.035
Oh, no, no, no, no.

36:04.328 --> 36:06.622
- Nora, you're gonna fucking die!
- [Nora grunting]

36:08.082 --> 36:09.249
[Ellie] Nora!

36:09.250 --> 36:10.418
[panting]

36:17.216 --> 36:19.260
- [gunshot]
- [Nora grunting]

36:20.970 --> 36:22.388
- [thud]
- [creaking]

36:23.181 --> 36:24.347
- [grunting]
- [chains rattling]

36:24.348 --> 36:25.933
[elevator banging]

36:27.185 --> 36:28.644
[groaning]

36:30.897 --> 36:32.064
- [gunshot]
- [gasps]

36:33.107 --> 36:35.234
[gunshots]

36:37.445 --> 36:38.862
[W.L.F. soldier]
Fuck, it's open.

36:38.863 --> 36:40.488
The fucking shaft is open!

36:40.489 --> 36:43.033
- Seal off the hallway!
- [soldier] Back, back, back!

36:43.034 --> 36:45.953
[W.L.F. soldier]
[indistinct]
The shaft is open.

36:46.996 --> 36:49.040
[echoing thud]

36:51.667 --> 36:54.670
[♪ ominous music playing]

37:42.343 --> 37:45.346
[♪ ominous music
continues playing]

38:12.623 --> 38:14.749
[infected gasping faintly]

38:14.750 --> 38:16.794
[exhaling slowly]

38:20.506 --> 38:22.508
[breathing raggedly]

38:36.814 --> 38:38.691
[infected gasping loudly]

38:46.282 --> 38:48.284
[wheezing]

38:56.667 --> 38:58.669
[coughing in distance]

39:08.971 --> 39:10.973
[coughing continues]

39:21.067 --> 39:24.070
- [electricity buzzing]
- [coughing continues]

39:25.654 --> 39:27.656
[coughing increasing]

39:36.499 --> 39:38.501
[Nora coughing]

39:45.132 --> 39:47.051
[straining]
You stupid bitch.

39:47.968 --> 39:50.303
Spores.
[groaning]

39:50.304 --> 39:52.515
We're breathing spores.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.267
We're infected.

39:56.268 --> 39:57.895
You killed us both.

39:58.646 --> 39:59.647
Did I?

40:01.649 --> 40:03.651
[wheezing]

40:12.076 --> 40:15.079
You're... you're her.

40:17.957 --> 40:20.417
The immune girl, you're...
[wheezing]

40:20.418 --> 40:21.836
You're real.

40:24.505 --> 40:25.506
Yeah.

40:27.049 --> 40:28.634
Where's Abby?

40:32.304 --> 40:34.306
Don't you know what he did?

40:35.724 --> 40:39.103
- I don't care.
- You don't care?

40:40.896 --> 40:45.192
He killed everyone
in that hospital.

40:46.819 --> 40:49.112
Including the only
fucking person alive

40:49.113 --> 40:51.031
that could make a cure
from you.

40:54.368 --> 40:56.078
That was Abby's father.

40:57.872 --> 40:59.165
And Joel...

41:00.541 --> 41:03.377
Joel shot him in the head.

41:05.004 --> 41:06.881
That's what he did.

41:12.845 --> 41:14.472
I know.

41:15.681 --> 41:16.765
[gasps]

41:17.141 --> 41:18.142
Oh...

41:18.559 --> 41:19.601
[scoffs]

41:19.602 --> 41:21.979
[♪ ominous music continues]

41:36.202 --> 41:37.619
Where's Abby?

41:37.620 --> 41:39.580
[coughing]

41:44.210 --> 41:45.211
No.

41:57.598 --> 41:59.600
[shallow breathing]

42:02.102 --> 42:04.104
[metal scraping]

42:18.744 --> 42:20.496
Where is she?

42:24.750 --> 42:25.834
No.

42:27.044 --> 42:29.046
- [Ellie shouting]
- [Nora screaming]

42:30.839 --> 42:32.841
[Nora whimpering]

42:33.717 --> 42:35.009
Where is she?

42:35.010 --> 42:36.219
[struggling] No.

42:36.220 --> 42:38.222
- [shouting]
- [screaming]

42:40.349 --> 42:41.808
Where is she?!

42:41.809 --> 42:43.811
- [metal scraping]
- [Ellie yelling]

42:52.403 --> 42:54.405
[birdsong]

42:59.577 --> 43:01.579
[door opening, creaking]

43:10.212 --> 43:11.463
Hey, kiddo.

43:12.214 --> 43:13.340
[distant dog barking]

43:15.301 --> 43:16.302
Hi.

43:19.013 --> 43:22.016
[♪ "Present Tense"
by Pearl Jam playing]

43:32.610 --> 43:37.448
♪ Do you see the way
that tree bends? ♪

43:40.159 --> 43:44.330
♪ Does it inspire? ♪

43:47.583 --> 43:52.755
♪ Leaning out
to catch the sun's rays ♪

43:54.131 --> 43:59.303
♪ A lesson to be applied ♪

44:02.848 --> 44:08.811
♪ Are you gettin'
somethin' out of this ♪

44:08.812 --> 44:15.109
♪ All encompassing trip ♪

44:15.110 --> 44:17.154
[♪ song fades out]
